    "created_at": "2023-04-05T01:29:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-04-05T01:29:09Z",
    "body": "The question here is whether the URL is observable at all, and thus we need to pass it in, or whether it'd suffice to use about:blank.\r\n\r\nTentatively, I think we should pass it in, because I can imagine other parts of the spec accessing the resulting document's URL, or resulting environment settings object's creation URL. It's not observable to JavaScript directly, but perhaps some other algorithm relies on it.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, for cases like error documents, I suspect in implementations they have URLs like `about:error` or something...\r\n\r\nThoughts welcome.",
